          "kind": "note",
          "data": {
            "text": "## Record and replay\n\n**Recording** plays an IQ file back as if it were a radio. Pick a file on it to start: nothing else here needs hardware.\n\n**Scope** draws the file's spectrum. Scrub the Recording node and the waterfall follows.\n\n**Channel** demodulates one signal out of it.\n\n**Baseband scope** shows the channel's constellation and eye. This is how you tell a locked decoder from a guessing one.\n\n**Baseband recorder** keeps just that channel, already down-converted, which is far smaller than the whole band.\n\n**Time machine** holds the last 30 seconds of IQ. Arm it, and when you hear something you missed you can replay it without having recorded the whole session.\n\n**Speaker** plays the audio."
          },
          "position": { "x": 0.0, "y": 700.0 }
